WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.107 --> 00:00:01.706
- You know if you're
having like curry and rice

00:00:01.706 --> 00:00:03.531
and you mix the perfect bite together,

00:00:03.531 --> 00:00:04.783
that's what it tastes like.

00:00:04.783 --> 00:00:08.033
(upbeat playful music)

00:00:08.915 --> 00:00:11.765
- Today we are going to
make Hyderabadi Biryani.

00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:12.787
It is a traditional dish.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:14.890
It's made in the technique of Dum Pukht.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.011
It's just spicy and it's full of flavors.

00:00:17.011 --> 00:00:19.961
It's more of a festive dish in our family.

00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:22.099
My son here is going to cook with me.

00:00:22.099 --> 00:00:23.495
- I really, really love Biryani.

00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:26.012
It's like probably one of
my favorite dishes ever.

00:00:26.012 --> 00:00:27.564
- I've never made Biryani before.

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:28.902
- I've always had my
mom to cook it for me.

00:00:28.902 --> 00:00:30.017
If you see all these ingredients,

00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:31.748
it looks like most Indian
food is really complicated

00:00:31.748 --> 00:00:33.130
and has a whole bunch of spices.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.305
- I've cooked a bunch with my mom,

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:36.412
so I'm pretty confident
I can follow along.

00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:39.536
- She is fun, but she's
kind of lazy sometimes.

00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:42.045
I like pampering her but
now she learn herself.

00:00:42.045 --> 00:00:44.373
- So we're gonna get started
with making the rice.

00:00:44.373 --> 00:00:47.017
While the rice is cooking,
we are going to do

00:00:47.017 --> 00:00:49.467
the preparation for the
gravy or the curry of it.

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.400
You got it?

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:51.359
So we're gonna heat the water,

00:00:51.359 --> 00:00:54.756
we have rice here, it's
approximately a cup full of rice

00:00:54.756 --> 00:00:55.789
and it's washed.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:01:00.647
We are going to put the
rice into a pot of water.

00:01:00.647 --> 00:01:01.574
- To make Chicken Biryani,

00:01:01.574 --> 00:01:03.105
first you prepare the
chicken, marinate it.

00:01:03.105 --> 00:01:06.522
Take three teaspoons of the vegan butter.

00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:11.482
And we add spices to it.

00:01:11.482 --> 00:01:12.315
We need garlic.

00:01:12.315 --> 00:01:13.227
- This is garlic, right?

00:01:13.227 --> 00:01:14.093
- Yes.

00:01:14.093 --> 00:01:14.926
- (laughing)

00:01:14.926 --> 00:01:15.759
- And give me a knife.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:16.592
And then you see we grated the ginger.

00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:18.780
Three teaspoon of garam masala.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:19.785
Half teaspoon...

00:01:19.785 --> 00:01:21.402
- There's cinnamon in Biryani?

00:01:21.402 --> 00:01:22.554
I would not have expected.

00:01:22.554 --> 00:01:24.379
- One teaspoon salt.

00:01:24.379 --> 00:01:26.298
- I have worked with
the spices a little bit.

00:01:26.298 --> 00:01:27.908
Normally my mom will mix them all

00:01:27.908 --> 00:01:29.380
into a little container for me,

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.581
like take one spoon of this spice mix

00:01:31.581 --> 00:01:33.370
and put it in my food.
So I don't have to really

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.913
think about it too much.

00:01:34.913 --> 00:01:36.462
- So we take the cilantro and mint,

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:39.545
and we chop it into very fine pieces.

00:01:43.696 --> 00:01:45.853
Mix it, we're making like a paste

00:01:45.853 --> 00:01:48.075
so you can put a little
bit of water in there.

00:01:48.075 --> 00:01:50.028
So basically what we do,
is we take the chicken

00:01:50.028 --> 00:01:53.096
and we stab it a little bit.

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:55.199
So now you see, we are
marinating the chicken.

00:01:55.199 --> 00:01:58.589
In Indian cooking, a lot
of it is love and affection

00:01:58.589 --> 00:02:00.431
that you give to the chicken.

00:02:00.431 --> 00:02:04.598
- You got marinade on my phone. (laughing)

00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:12.700
- Now we are going to take some salt,

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.950
put like a quarter spoon, teaspoon.

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.667
Let's put two bay leaves in it.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.771
- They give a nice flavor to it.

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:20.214
And then we put four cloves.

00:02:20.214 --> 00:02:22.164
- How many did you put?

00:02:22.164 --> 00:02:23.395
- I put around five of them.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:26.563
Let's snap this into two
because this is pretty big.

00:02:26.563 --> 00:02:28.008
We'll put some cinnamon in it.

00:02:28.008 --> 00:02:29.606
- So you take the cardamom out here first

00:02:29.606 --> 00:02:31.070
and then we crush them.

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:33.386
- How are you doing that so easily?

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:37.099
- You just open it, just
like you open a peanut.

00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:40.855
- Now this is all
seasoned, let's close it.

00:02:40.855 --> 00:02:43.270
Put the heat on little bit more than hot.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.892
- Just fry them a little bit

00:02:44.892 --> 00:02:46.841
with a little bit of mixed nuts.

00:02:46.841 --> 00:02:49.063
When the cumin is roasting a little,

00:02:49.063 --> 00:02:51.202
then you just put all the rice

00:02:51.202 --> 00:02:54.015
and fry the rice a little bit.

00:02:54.015 --> 00:02:55.848
So go ahead and saute.

00:02:57.504 --> 00:03:00.924
- So far so good (laughing) yeah.

00:03:00.924 --> 00:03:02.462
- So while this is gonna cook,

00:03:02.462 --> 00:03:05.362
let's talk preparing the vegetables.

00:03:05.362 --> 00:03:06.417
See, that's how good he is.

00:03:06.417 --> 00:03:08.049
He knows how to do the onions.

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:10.210
- In this, we usually
put two medium onions.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.460
Yeah, don't make too small.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.161
(chopping)

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:17.276
- So it kinda came apart.

00:03:17.276 --> 00:03:18.233
- (whispering) Yes!

00:03:18.233 --> 00:03:19.066
Done!

00:03:19.066 --> 00:03:21.415
- (laughing) he's got
more practice than I have.

00:03:21.415 --> 00:03:24.474
- That just means I have to
do all the cutting at home.

00:03:24.474 --> 00:03:26.599
- Did you already do
your whole onion? Oh man.

00:03:26.599 --> 00:03:28.568
- Of course I'm waiting for
him to bring a girl home.

00:03:28.568 --> 00:03:32.728
Look, I've taught him well. (laughing)

00:03:32.728 --> 00:03:35.069
- So the chicken has been
marinated for an hour.

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:36.828
Let's take the marinated chicken

00:03:36.828 --> 00:03:38.874
and we put it like this.

00:03:38.874 --> 00:03:41.124
(sizzling)

00:03:42.198 --> 00:03:45.144
- Alright so, we will put some ghee.

00:03:45.144 --> 00:03:47.076
Ghee is purified butter, it's like love.

00:03:47.076 --> 00:03:49.674
- Every time you say cardamom,
you wanna say lychee.

00:03:49.674 --> 00:03:51.958
But you like stop and
then you're like cardamom.

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:53.167
- What is haldi in English?

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.000
- Tumeric.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.779
- I have to like Google
what something is in English

00:03:55.779 --> 00:03:58.029
so I can buy it at a store.

00:03:59.043 --> 00:04:00.735
- (laughing)

00:04:00.735 --> 00:04:02.152
Nice, nice, nice.

00:04:03.105 --> 00:04:03.938
- Beans?

00:04:03.938 --> 00:04:06.770
- I am putting the beans in.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.919
Now let's put some yogurt.

00:04:08.919 --> 00:04:10.016
- Normally, we're like cooking, she's like

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.934
"So how's like the job
applications going?"

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.484
and like where's this and where's that.

00:04:13.484 --> 00:04:16.276
So I'm like forced to be
here and be interrogated.

00:04:16.276 --> 00:04:17.817
- Answer my question!

00:04:17.817 --> 00:04:20.734
- It's cooked on one side, flip it.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.569
- Alright, so I think
our vegetables are done.

00:04:25.569 --> 00:04:28.045
Now we are going to do Dum Pukht of it.

00:04:28.045 --> 00:04:30.128
We have some heated milk.

00:04:31.148 --> 00:04:32.590
So the warm milk and the saffron

00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.636
is just going to release
the flavor and the color.

00:04:34.636 --> 00:04:37.823
- Now you put like one
spoon of rice in a layer.

00:04:37.823 --> 00:04:40.785
- We'll put some cilantro.

00:04:40.785 --> 00:04:43.705
Let's spread the layer of rice.

00:04:43.705 --> 00:04:46.247
- Then you put your chicken on top of it.

00:04:46.247 --> 00:04:48.790
I'm gonna top it with rice.

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.292
So you check it, like a little bit of rice

00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:52.133
and see if it's cooked.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.900
- And so we're gonna
leave it for 20 minutes

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.744
and it's ready to sow.

00:04:55.744 --> 00:04:57.769
- (applause) Yay!

00:04:57.769 --> 00:04:59.247
- Okay, so which one is yours now?

00:04:59.247 --> 00:05:01.315
- See, you can't tell,
that means it's good.

00:05:01.315 --> 00:05:02.732
So this is yours.

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.473
That's really good.

00:05:04.473 --> 00:05:07.660
- Yours looks more covered
in saffron than mine.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.308
- So tastes like Biryani,
like good Biryani.

00:05:10.308 --> 00:05:11.637
